    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493296238/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Friday Dec. 16. 1898. Frullino. Florence.
We had a most divine walk – an old Fiesole “rampart walk”. The day was en - chant - ing. A telegram came from Alys saying that Benjamin Frank Conn Costelloe [written: B.F.C.C.] will not make trouble if I put off my home-coming till the 10th. As I  might  not have been able to go at all, this is a pure gain, and it made me happy. But I was happy anyhow with Bernhard and the sunshine. 
Fairchild came and gave me a lesson, and at 7.15 I met Trevy who arrived from England with a heavy bag of books. He was very nice in the evening."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 116 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1898-99> .

